	(paper "A4")
	(lib_symbols)
	(text "XLR/Mic levels are low (-60 dBu to -30dBu) and have low impedances(~150 to 600 ohms)\ntherefore, their gain stages require the highest amount of preamp. (+30dB to +60dB of gain)\nnoise within the preamp circuit will also be amplified, low self-noise is critical\n\nTS (Instrument) levels are moderate, (-30dbU to -10dbU) and have high impedance (Hi-Z, ~1Mohm)\ntherefore, their gain stages require moderate preamp. (+10dB to +30dB of gain)\ntransients are a concern, as well as EMI/RFI pickup over longer cable distances\n\nTS (Line) levels are high, (-10dbV / ~-7.78dBu), and have medium impedances (10k to 40k). \ntherefore, their gain stages require little to no preamp."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
